#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/id #uuid "e95210c5-adb4-519e-bbec-e240dac32fd8" :question/math-academy-id "e-3614" :question/problem "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin 15^{∘}\\cos 15^{∘} &= \\sin (2 \\cdot 15^{∘}) = \\sin 30^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059423 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/id #uuid "35535b08-b3d8-5037-a821-6815577169d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-3618" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})]\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\n$$\n\nwe can further simplify the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[\\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\sin (\\frac{π}{6}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059424 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/id #uuid "b03496ac-c3b2-5d65-a3e3-2a33ea0cb862" :question/math-academy-id "e-3619" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{\\sin 50^{∘}} &= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sec 25^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "539b5b86-7b31-52c9-be04-e80d6799b68a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3623" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{8}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 2\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}} = 3 \\left(\\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4483a191-ab5f-53cc-9a25-631101495ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256212} {:answer/id #uuid "1bca9c9f-347e-50cd-983a-012520b04ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256213} {:answer/id #uuid "7182fa70-cf00-5a72-8698-deb11fabc8da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256214} {:answer/id #uuid "be86f2e5-0b3d-52c0-a00f-2a4b04f18b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256215} {:answer/id #uuid "4b12d860-258e-5359-827c-56ef56e1e69d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be86f2e5-0b3d-52c0-a00f-2a4b04f18b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256215} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4715576-2b79-520b-9527-45c19ddc2f36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9834bdc8-d968-5825-adae-a20e0fb4ec63" :question/math-academy-id "q-119948" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10}) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4bffe8b-3637-547c-99be-c2ee069ca61c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256254} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b9e4e0-fa4d-5e47-b517-e31db15c125f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256255} {:answer/id #uuid "ed742626-ab3e-5908-9345-2200a481d3f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256256} {:answer/id #uuid "7b163501-27d4-56be-b447-5a3ccfd8d07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256257} {:answer/id #uuid "0446b95c-c2af-560d-abd1-109cb4fc118a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b163501-27d4-56be-b447-5a3ccfd8d07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256257} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bb793c7-2ed0-5340-b770-f69725fc53fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04ad99db-b562-50ab-884b-fce6f7ff1c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-24647" :question/problem "Express $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c89a54-fb37-5e7f-b93d-ebbdffe60694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256275} {:answer/id #uuid "75fef84a-4659-5182-9dc8-65882bb13b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c89a54-fb37-5e7f-b93d-ebbdffe60694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256275} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b960d8-b823-521f-ba0a-f080d7d65c62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "62770764-8176-56e9-8c60-1a1dcb94a9d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-327716" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a4ec08-4df2-504b-8bb2-165aa83be092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21a4ec08-4df2-504b-8bb2-165aa83be092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256279} :answer-field/id #uuid "341f39aa-6a81-5083-8264-e503b649bf89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c3ab403-d373-50aa-ab7d-cad9629d8aab" :question/math-academy-id "q-327763" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}).$\n\n$14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =7\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})) \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6c2ebd8-fdbf-5b5b-8ba1-8fc5fd77a0e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256302} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1196b0-4c7c-5880-9caf-53995ca6623b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256303} {:answer/id #uuid "62346b99-48f0-5873-bfe4-a384b2655b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256304} {:answer/id #uuid "30b3b57a-350b-57aa-9671-d921d8ac88f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{14})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256305} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb68c40-7670-55f8-9bb2-511ad8765fcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62346b99-48f0-5873-bfe4-a384b2655b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256304} :answer-field/id #uuid "3322114a-016d-5a3a-81f3-c9d23de58d6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dffc7ff8-f6d1-5483-ae2f-efbd6a7d92e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-7305" :question/problem "Express $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{7})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{7})$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{7}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{7})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{7}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{7})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{7}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d312bf9-58c7-5520-9129-0703c48a8cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256323} {:answer/id #uuid "727c4412-3cd6-58fc-99d1-47790c9ac038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256324} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfd7587-fda4-51d3-bbfd-8910552cadef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256325} {:answer/id #uuid "fc157362-2a60-5606-98ba-80157755256c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256326} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4a2b50-b885-56c1-8cf9-e70be04d1f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc157362-2a60-5606-98ba-80157755256c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256326} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9834f55-f2fa-503d-b373-f1d8df6fecf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dbcaa5c5-944e-50c6-9be1-0fbde394c6c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-7676" :question/problem "Express $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{28}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{28}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting $x={28}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{28}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{28}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {28}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}.\n$$"}]}
